{%- comment -%}
  Bush Riding ethos — the brand story, set dense.

  This section exists because the home page read as unfinished: four sections,
  each saying one short thing, with the page's full width unused. The answer is
  not more padding tricks, it is more substance, laid out tight.

  Three movements, deliberately different shapes so the eye keeps moving:

    1. The lead — what the gear is for. A statement, then three supporting
       lines running in columns beside it rather than under it.
    2. The country — one line per landscape, as a numbered ledger across two
       or three columns. Hairline-separated, numerals in khaki. This is the
       block that does the most work against empty space.
    3. The passage — the drovers, then the turn. Two columns of body copy,
       read left to right.

  Copy lives in settings and blocks, so the words can change without a deploy.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ground = section.settings.ground | default: 'bone'
-%}

<section class="alp alp-ethos alp-ethos--{{ ground }}" id="ethos" aria-label="{{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: 'Ethos' | escape }}">
  <div class="alp-ethos__inner">
    <div class="alp-ethos__lead alp-reveal">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="alp-ethos__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.statement != blank -%}
        <h2 class="alp-ethos__statement">{{ section.settings.statement | escape }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
        <div class="alp-ethos__intro">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.country_line != blank -%}
      <p class="alp-ethos__country alp-reveal">{{ section.settings.country_line | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ol class="alp-ethos__ledger" role="list">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          <li class="alp-ethos__row alp-reveal" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- comment -%}
              The numeral is decoration, not content — the line reads the same
              without it, and a screen reader shouldn't count the weather.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="alp-ethos__n" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</span>
            <p class="alp-ethos__line">{{ block.settings.text | escape }}</p>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ol>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.passage_a != blank or section.settings.passage_b != blank -%}
      <div class="alp-ethos__passage alp-reveal">
        {%- if section.settings.passage_a != blank -%}
          <div class="alp-ethos__col">{{ section.settings.passage_a }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.passage_b != blank -%}
          <div class="alp-ethos__col">{{ section.settings.passage_b }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Bush Riding ethos",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "ground",
      "label": "Ground",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bone", "label": "Bone — content ground, reads as a panel on the mist page" },
        { "value": "mist", "label": "Mist — continuous with the home page" },
        { "value": "olive", "label": "Olive — dark slab, bone type" }
      ],
      "default": "bone"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Made for the detour" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "statement",
      "label": "Statement",
      "default": "Bush Riding designs are made for riding a bike through the Australian Bush."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "intro",
      "label": "Intro",
      "default": "<p>We make gear for those who feel drawn to adventure and the unknown.</p><p>Allowing for comfortable exploration in one of our planet's most unforgiving climates.</p><p>For those who embark on a journey through the Aussie bush, better come prepared.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The country" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "country_line",
      "label": "Opening line",
      "default": "Our country is vast, breath-taking and at times, unforgiving."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each landscape below is a block. Add, reorder or remove them — the numerals renumber themselves."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The passage" },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "passage_a",
      "label": "Left column",
      "default": "<p>For centuries, people traversed this land atop a saddle.</p><p>Trusting their steed to confidently navigate the unforgiving terrain and arid climate.</p><p>Years spent droving, leaving behind the trails we still ride today.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "passage_b",
      "label": "Right column",
      "default": "<p>We've swapped the steed for a steel frame and the drover's swag for a bar bag.</p><p>We ride the same dirt, chase the same horizons, seek the same shelter.</p><p>Because somewhere beyond the city limits, the noise falls away.</p><p>The road narrows. The surface softens and the country opens up.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "line",
      "name": "Landscape",
      "settings": [{ "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Line" }]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 12,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Bush Riding ethos",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "line", "settings": { "text": "Sweltering summer storms electrocute the sky and clap our ears with thunder." } },
        { "type": "line", "settings": { "text": "Ancient river red gums groan and creak, whispering secrets older than the trails beneath them." } },
        { "type": "line", "settings": { "text": "Icy mountain mornings bite our fingers and fog our breath before the warm sun crests the horizon." } },
        { "type": "line", "settings": { "text": "Coastal cliffs roar with salt spray, drowning our thoughts beneath crashing swell." } },
        { "type": "line", "settings": { "text": "Rainforest canopies drip and hum, drenching our skin in humidity thick enough to taste." } },
        { "type": "line", "settings": { "text": "Star-choked outback skies swallow the darkness whole, humbling us beneath more light than we've ever known." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
